      "writtenOn": "2014-12-31T18:07:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m wondering if we could return \"Project ID not found\" even with debug\u003dFalse... if the username and password are validated first, then I don\u0027t see a problem with reporting that the project doesn\u0027t exist. For example, I could authenticate to project A as long as I provide the right password and I\u0027ve got a role on A so I know it exists. Then I try to authenticate to project B and it says 401 Unauthorized... so it either doesn\u0027t exist or I don\u0027t have a role on it... what\u0027s the danger of telling the user that project B doesn\u0027t exist or I don\u0027t have a role on it (as long as my password was validated first)?",
      "revId": "9fb4d0e9d2540f3d5bf7b3f2ce952d45181140f3",
